NiriFX for Arch Linux
====================

Open NiriFX Studio from your application launcher, or run:

    /usr/bin/niri-fx studio --active

Install Chromium for an app-style window. Otherwise Studio opens your default
browser. Niri is needed to validate and apply effects; preview and JSON export
also work without a running compositor. Quickshell and GTK pickers are optional.
Choose a preset for each action, review the proposed changes, then Apply.
Installing, upgrading or removing this package does not apply effects.

This package contains the released CLI, Studio, preset library and integrations.
It does not include the patched compositor or add a NiriFX login session.
Stock Niri supports the documented open/close/resize effects; continuous drag,
custom movement and swaps require the separately prepared full NiriFX session.
No stock Niri, shell, service or user configuration files are replaced.

Updates and existing managed sessions
------------------------------------

Update this package using your normal AUR workflow. Reopen Studio to use the
updated package; refreshing a page does not replace its running server.
System Python minor-version updates can require rebuilding AUR Python packages.

An existing managed NiriFX session uses retained virtual environments so that
its selected and previous tools survive package updates. This package does not
replace those environments or switch their launchers. Do not use /usr/bin/python
as a managed tools runtime, upgrade a retained environment in place, or remove
retained files to resolve a package/launcher mismatch.

If a user-installed niri-fx or Studio launcher takes precedence over this package,
it remains in place. Use /usr/bin/niri-fx explicitly to test the packaged tools.
Use the reviewed managed-tool workflow to update an existing full session:

https://github.com/jturbide/niri-fx/blob/v0.21.0/docs/tool-updates.md

Recovery
--------

Use Studio Restore for effects applied by the standalone tools. Removing the
package leaves your effects, saved profiles and Restore history in place; restore
effects before removal if you want the underlying configuration back. Native
session rollback is a separate reviewed operation. Keep stock Niri available.

Portable examples: /usr/share/doc/niri-fx/examples/
Versioned documentation: https://github.com/jturbide/niri-fx/tree/v0.21.0/docs
Source and issues: https://github.com/jturbide/niri-fx
